+// A quadratic Bernstein axis is an arbitrary separating-plane candidate,
+// not an assertion that the computed cross product is exact. Project ORIGINAL
+// affine endpoints onto its stored high/low coefficients with outward intervals.
+// Their cubic Bernstein coefficients enclose every pairwise projection for the
+// entire sweep. Norm convexity bounds the axis length by its three control norms.
+// Strict lower bounds for all coefficients therefore certify the SAME clearance,
+// while allowing the separating plane to rotate with deforming thin features.
+inline bool nmReferenceContactPolynomialSweepSeparated(
+    uint kind,thread const MRCompensatedPositionGPU* start,
+    thread const MRCompensatedPositionGPU* finish,float3 normal,float clearance) {
+    if(!isfinite(clearance)||!(clearance>0.0f))return false;
+    uint firstCount=1u,secondBegin=1u,secondCount=1u;
+    MRCompensatedPositionGPU axis[3];
